Statement	Meaning
STOP RUN	     Terminates the entire COBOL run unit
GOBACK	       Returns to the caller, or terminates if there is no caller
EXIT PROGRAM	 Returns control from a called program to its caller

Example:
- Main Program: Usually uses STOP RUN to end execution.
- Subprogram: Usually uses GOBACK to return control.
- EXIT PROGRAM: Can be used when a Subprogram needs to return to its caller without terminating the run unit.

Interview answer: We generally use GOBACK in a Subprogram because STOP RUN would terminate the entire application instead of just returning to the Main Program.
